      "content": "That makes sense. It's essentially a mechanical failure of the cell structure that triggers the chemical release. I'm just trying to find a way to help the students conceptualize that \"unpredictable\" or \"mischievous\" quality of the sensation—how it feels like something is working against you. Is there any part of the reaction's kinetics or the way the gas spreads that could be described in a way that captures that sense of sudden, irritating chaos?",
